1
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Cable Hogue says … “Do unto others … as you would have others do unto you.”

2
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:12,000
The Ballad of Cable Hogue is a comedy, western,
action film directed by Sam Peckinpah.

3
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:15,000
Double-crossed and left without water in the desert,
Cable Hogue is saved when he finds a spring.

4
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:18,000
It is in just the right spot for a much needed rest stop on the local
stagecoach line, and Hogue uses this to his advantage.

5
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:21,000
He builds a house and makes money off the stagecoach passengers.

6
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:24,000
Hildy, a prostitute from the nearest town, moves in with him.

7
00:42:21,000 --> 00:42:27,000
Hogue has everything going his way until the advent of the
automobile ends the era of the stagecoach.

8
00:48:24,000 --> 00:48:30,000
Cable Hogue, played by Jason Robards.

9
00:54:27,000 --> 00:54:33,000
Hildy, played by Stella Stevens.

10
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Ben Fairchild, played by Slim Pickens.

11
01:06:33,000 --> 01:06:39,000
Joshua, played by David Warner.

12
01:12:36,000 --> 01:12:42,000
Taggart, played by L.Q. Jones.

13
01:18:39,000 --> 01:18:45,000
Bowen, played by Strother Martin.

14
01:24:42,000 --> 01:24:48,000
The Ballad of Cable Hogue is a 1970 American Technicolor Western comedy film directed by
Sam Peckinpah and starring Jason Robards, Stella Stevens and David Warner.

15
01:30:45,000 --> 01:30:51,000
Set in the Arizona desert during a period when the frontier was closing, the
film follows three years in the life of a failed prospector.

16
01:36:48,000 --> 01:36:54,000
While unmistakably a Western, the movie is
unconventional for the genre and for the director.

17
01:42:51,000 --> 01:42:57,000
It contains only a few brief scenes of violence and gunplay, relying more on a subtly
crafted story that could better be characterized as comedic in nature.

18
01:48:54,000 --> 01:49:00,000
The film explores themes of prostitute, homeless
person, desert, stagecoach, prospector.

19
01:54:57,000 --> 01:55:03,000
The tone is lighthearted.
